{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_019CThHoWLhUJZWjh2Qqkcby","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"issues\":{\"nodes\":[{\"expand\":\"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations\",\"id\":\"578865\",\"self\":\"https://api.atlassian.com/ex/jira/88b0b656-d57e-42ea-87c1-2808cc792710/rest/api/3/issue/578865\",\"key\":\"TARS-1351\",\"fields\":{\"summary\":\"Module runbook: Placements\",\"issuetype\":{\"self\":\"https://api.atlassian.com/ex/jira/88b0b656-d57e-42ea-87c1-2808cc792710/rest/api/3/issuetype/11513\",\"id\":\"11513\",\"description\":\"Inventory issue for software that is internally developed and packaged - but deployed *WITHIN* a different application\",\"iconUrl\":\"https://api.atlassian.com/ex/jira/88b0b656-d57e-42ea-87c1-2808cc792710/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/11316?size=medium\",\"name\":\"Internal Package Software\",\"subtask\":false,\"avatarId\":11316,\"hierarchyLevel\":0},\"components\":[{\"self\":\"https://api.atlassian.com/ex/jira/88b0b656-d57e-42ea-87c1-2808cc792710/rest/api/3/component/16285\",\"id\":\"16285\",\"name\":\"tars-placement\"},{\"self\":\"https://api.atlassian.com/ex/jira/88b0b656-d57e-42ea-87c1-2808cc792710/rest/api/3/component/18435\",\"id\":\"18435\",\"name\":\"webtarsthree\"}],\"created\":\"2026-08-01T13:05:21.078-0700\",\"description\":\"Bring `docs/modules/placements.md` up to a runbook that Product and Devs can both use for the **Placements** module.\\n\\nThis is documentation only. No client or server code changes.\\n\\n## Current state\\n\\n* `docs/modules/placements.md` exists at 74 lines, with these sections: `## Purpose`, `## Access`, `## Features`, `## External Services`, `## Key Business Rules`, `## Structure`, `## Working Here`.\\n* `## Client Routes`: **missing**. The module serves 12 client route(s).\\n* `## Server Routes`: **missing**. `src/server/app.js` registers 15 `/api/placements` endpoint(s).\\n* `## Prerequisites`: **missing** — no module doc has one yet.\\n* The doc points developers at `src/server/index.js` for route wiring. That is wrong: `src/server/index.js` is an 18-line listener, and all routes are registered in `src/server/app.js`.\\n\\n## What to write\\n\\n* **What the module is** — what Placements does and who uses it.\\n* **Pages / routes** — a table of every client route and what that page does.\\n* **Server routes** — a table of each endpoint, its handler, and its purpose.\\n* **Prerequisites** — the AD group needed for access (none — any authenticated user), plus every service this module is hooked up to.\\n* **Current-state overview** — how the module works today, not how it should work.\\n\\nKeep it a general runbook for Product and Devs. Do not narrate individual files or walk through code.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n* `docs/modules/placements.md` has a `## Client Routes` section AND every one of the 12 client route(s) below appears in the file — verify with: `grep -q \\\"^## Client Routes\\\" docs/modules/placements.md && for p in /placements /placements/playground /placements/create /placements/browse /placements/browse/1 /placements/browse/:folderId /placements/scheduler /placements/scheduler/form/:slug /placements/scheduler/json/:slug /placements/scheduler/list/:slug /placements/scheduler/fd-list/:slug /placements/scheduler/fd-list-fid/:slug; do grep -q \\\"$p\\\" docs/modules/placements.md || exit 1; done`\\n* `docs/modules/placements.md` has a `## Server Routes` section covering the 15 `/api/placements` endpoint(s) registered in `src/server/app.js` — verify with: `grep -q \\\"^## Server Routes\\\" docs/modules/placements.md`\\n* `docs/modules/placements.md` has a `## Prerequisites` section naming the AD group required to reach `/placements` and every external service the module calls — verify with: `grep -q \\\"^## Prerequisites\\\" docs/modules/placements.md`\\n* `docs/modules/placements.md` still has every section it has today (`## Purpose`, `## Access`, `## Features`, `## External Services`, `## Key Business Rules`, `## Structure`, `## Working Here`) — nothing is deleted to make room — verify with: `for h in \\\"Purpose\\\" \\\"Access\\\" \\\"Features\\\" \\\"External Services\\\" \\\"Key Business Rules\\\" \\\"Structure\\\" \\\"Working Here\\\"; do grep -q \\\"^## $h\\\" docs/modules/placements.md || exit 1; done`\\n* `docs/modules/placements.md` no longer tells developers to wire routes in `src/server/index.js` — that file is an 18-line listener and every route is registered in `src/server/app.js` — verify with: `! grep -q \\\"src/server/index.js\\\" docs/modules/placements.md`\\n* The repository test suite still passes — verify with: `npm test`\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\n* Any change under `src/`.\\n* Renaming or moving the doc.\\n\\n\",\"project\":{\"self\":\"https://api.atlassian.com/ex/jira/88b0b656-d57e-42ea-87c1-2808cc792710/rest/api/3/project/12510\",\"id\":\"12510\",\"key\":\"TARS\",\"name\":\"TARS\",\"projectTypeKey\":\"software\",\"simplified\":false,\"avatarUrls\":{\"48x48\":\"https://api.atlassian.com/ex/jira/88b0b656-d57e-42ea-87c1-2808cc792710/rest/api/3/universal_avatar/view/type/project/avatar/17301\",\"24x24\":\"https://api.atlassian.com/ex/jira/88b0b656-d57e-42ea-87c1-2808cc792710/rest/api/3/universal_avatar/view/type/project/avatar/17301?size=small\",\"16x16\":\"https://api.atlassian.com/ex/jira/88b0b656-d57e-42ea-87c1-2808cc792710/rest/api/3/universal_avatar/view/type/project/avatar/17301?size=xsmall\",\"32x32\":\"https://api.atlassian.com/ex/jira/88b0b656-d57e-42ea-87c1-2808cc792710/rest/api/3/universal_avatar/view/type/project/avatar/17301?size=medium\"},\"projectCategory\":{\"self\":\"https://api.atlassian.com/ex/jira/88b0b656-d57e-42ea-87c1-2808cc792710/rest/api/3/projectCategory/11009\",\"id\":\"11009\",\"description\":\"Software that gets build into a versioned artifact and deployed to our various environments: https://fandango.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ATJ/pages/1729692229