{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_011tpMQxfn4dUJvvGSXMp5yh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Placements\n2\t\n3\t## Purpose\n4\t\n5\tManages content placements for Fandango properties. Provides tools for scheduling, organizing, and previewing editorial content placements across different platform surfaces.\n6\t\n7\t## Access\n8\t\n9\t- **Route:** `/placements`\n10\t- **AD Group:** None — available to all authenticated users\n11\t\n12\t## Features\n13\t\n14\t**Scheduler**\n15\t\n16\t- View and manage placement schedules by slug\n17\t- Create, duplicate, and delete schedule items\n18\t- Clone entire placements\n19\t- Update placement metadata and schemas\n20\t- View live content for a placement\n21\t- Look up item metadata by content type and EMS ID\n22\t\n23\t**Browse / Folders**\n24\t\n25\t- Browse placements organized in folders\n26\t- Create, update, and delete folders\n27\t- Add placements to folders\n28\t\n29\t**Playground**\n30\t\n31\t- Preview and test placement configurations\n32\t\n33\t## External Services\n34\t\n35\t| Service           | Purpose                                      | Env Var                      |\n36\t| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n37\t| Placement Service | Core CRUD for placements, schedules, folders | `PLACEMENT_SERVICE_ENDPOINT` |\n38\t\n39\t## Key Business Rules\n40\t\n41\t- **Slugs:** Placements are identified by slug (URL-friendly identifier), not numeric IDs.\n42\t- **Schemas:** Each placement has a configurable schema that defines the shape of its content items.\n43\t- **Cloning:** Entire placements can be cloned for creating variations or staging.\n44\t- **Live content:** The scheduler shows what's currently live vs scheduled for each placement.\n45\t- **Folder organization:** Placements are organized into a folder hierarchy for browsing.\n46\t\n47\t## Structure\n48\t\n49\t- Client: `src/client/pages/placements/` — `scheduler/`, `folders/`, `playground/`, `_shared/`\n50\t- Server: `src/server/placements/` — `scheduler/`, `browse/`\n51\t\n52\t## Working Here\n53\t\n54\t**Module structure:**\n55\t\n56\tPlacements has three sub-features (scheduler, folders, playground) and shared utilities in `_shared/`. The shared folder contains components, hooks, drag utilities, RJSF (React JSON Schema Form) config, and a placement validator.\n57\t\n58\t**Read first:**\n59\t\n60\t1. `PlacementsPage.jsx` — landing page with placement list\n61\t2. `scheduler/SchedulerListPage.jsx` — the most complex sub-feature\n62\t3. `_shared/rjsfConfig.js` — RJSF configuration for schema-driven forms\n63\t4. `_shared/placementUtils.js` — shared utility functions\n64\t\n65\t**Adding a new placement feature:**\n66\t\n67\t1. Create `src/client/pages/placements/{feature}/` following `scheduler/` or `folders/` as reference\n68\t2. Add shared components to `_shared/components/` if reusable\n69\t3. Server handlers go in `src/server/placements/{feature}/`\n70\t4. Wire routes in `src/server/index.js` under the Placements section\n71\t\n72\t**Server-side pattern:**\n73\t\n74\tAll handlers call the Placement Service via `PLACEMENT_SERVICE_ENDPOINT`. Server is split into `scheduler/` and `browse/` matching the client-side feature split.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e77c916-bd20-4e4a-9aa4-d29922bf6a2f","uuid":"388d61cb-acf0-4897-9b35-2d610a32311e","timestamp":"2026-08-02T04:16:14.304Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/206618626@bwt3.com/Desktop/Repos/webtarsthree/docs/modules/placements.md","content":"# Placements\n\n## Purpose\n\nManages content placements for Fandango properties. Provides tools for scheduling, organizing, and previewing editorial content placements across different platform surfaces.\n\n## Access\n\n- **Route:** `/placements`\n- **AD Group:** None — available to all authenticated users\n\n## Features\n\n**Scheduler**\n\n- View and manage placement schedules by slug\n- Create, duplicate, and delete schedule items\n- Clone entire placements\n- Update placement metadata and schemas\n- View live content for a placement\n- Look up item metadata by content type and EMS ID\n\n**Browse / Folders**\n\n- Browse placements organized in folders\n- Create, update, and delete folders\n- Add placements to folders\n\n**Playground**\n\n- Preview and test placement configurations\n\n## External Services\n\n| Service           | Purpose                                      | Env Var                      |\n| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| Placement Service | Core CRUD for placements, schedules, folders | `PLACEMENT_SERVICE_ENDPOINT` |\n\n## Key Business Rules\n\n- **Slugs:** Placements are identified by slug (URL-friendly identifier), not numeric IDs.\n- **Schemas:** Each placement has a configurable schema that defines the shape of its content items.\n- **Cloning:** Entire placements can be cloned for creating variations or staging.\n- **Live content:** The scheduler shows what's currently live vs scheduled for each placement.\n- **Folder organization:** Placements are organized into a folder hierarchy for browsing.\n\n## Structure\n\n- Client: `src/client/pages/placements/` — `scheduler/`, `folders/`, `playground/`, `_shared/`\n- Server: `src/server/placements/` — `scheduler/`, `browse/`\n\n## Working Here\n\n**Module structure:**\n\nPlacements has three sub-features (scheduler, folders, playground) and shared utilities in `_shared/`. The shared folder contains components, hooks, drag utilities, RJSF (React JSON Schema Form) config, and a placement validator.\n\n**Read first:**\n\n1. `PlacementsPage.jsx` — landing page with placement list\n2. `scheduler/SchedulerListPage.jsx` — the most complex sub-feature\n3. `_shared/rjsfConfig.js` — RJSF configuration for schema-driven forms\n4. `_shared/placementUtils.js` — shared utility functions\n\n**Adding a new placement feature:**\n\n1. Create `src/client/pages/placements/{feature}/` following `scheduler/` or `folders/` as reference\n2. Add shared components to `_shared/components/` if reusable\n3. Server handlers go in `src/server/placements/{feature}/`\n4. Wire routes in `src/server/index.js` under the Placements section\n\n**Server-side pattern:**\n\nAll handlers call the Placement Service via `PLACEMENT_SERVICE_ENDPOINT`. Server is split into `scheduler/` and `browse/` matching the client-side feature split.\n","numLines":75,"startLine":1,"totalLines":75}}}
