{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"aff48a4b5080b27f3","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01WBt9W6zfNnbUuBbjZkdBRW","status":"completed","output_file":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-206618626-bwt3-com-Desktop-Repos-webtarsthree/9e77c916-bd20-4e4a-9aa4-d29922bf6a2f/tasks/aff48a4b5080b27f3.output","summary":"I have all the information needed. Here's the report:\n\n## 1. Client Routes (defined in `src/client/App.jsx`, lines 145-159, under `<Route path=\"/placements\" element={<ModuleLayout />}>`)\n\n| Path | Component | File | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `/placements` (index) | `PlacementsPage` | pages/placements/PlacementsPage.jsx | Landing page for the module; shows recent placement history with a \"clear history\" action. |\n| `/placements/create` | `PlacementsCreatePage` | pages/placements/PlacementsCreatePage.jsx | Form to create a new placement, choosing a type (form / list / fd-list / fd-list-fid). |\n| `/placements/playground` | `PlaygroundPage` | pages/placements/playground/PlaygroundPage.jsx | Sandbox to build/preview a JSON-schema + UI-schema and live-preview the generated form (no server persistence). |\n| `/placements/browse` (index) | redirect | — | Redirects to `/placements/browse/1` (root folder). |\n| `/placements/browse/1` , `/placements/browse/:folderId` | `PlacementsBrowsePage` | pages/placements/folders/PlacementsBrowsePage.jsx | Folder browser with drag-and-drop for organizing placements into folders/subfolders. |\n| `/placements/scheduler/form/:slug` | `SchedulerFormPage` | pages/placements/scheduler/SchedulerFormPage.jsx | Editor for a schema-driven \"form\" type placement — edit content/schema tabs, view live/scheduled/history. |\n| `/placements/scheduler/json/:slug` | `SchedulerJsonPage` | pages/placements/scheduler/SchedulerJsonPage.jsx | Raw JSON editor variant of the placement editor (content/schema tabs via JSON). |\n| `/placements/scheduler/list/:slug` | `SchedulerListPage` | pages/placements/scheduler/SchedulerListPage.jsx | Editor for \"list\" type placements — drag-and-drop ordered content list (also handles `fd-list`/`fd-list-fid` UI variants based on placement config). |\n| `/placements/scheduler/fd-list/:slug` | `SchedulerListPage` (same component) | same file | Same list editor, used for Fandango/Vudu-flavored list placements (`ui: 'fd-list'`). |\n| `/placements/scheduler/fd-list-fid/:slug` | `SchedulerListPage` (same component) | same file | Same list editor for the FID-lookup list variant (`ui: 'fd-list-fid'`, items resolved by Fandango ID). |\n\nLegacy `/schedule/*` paths also redirect into these placements routes (tars-2 backward-compat).\n\n## 2. Server Routes (`src/server/app.js` ~437-465)\n\n| Method + Path | Handler File | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| GET `/api/placements` | browse/placements.browse.getAllPlacements.js | Lists all placements, optional `?name=` filter, via Placement Service. |\n| POST `/api/placements` | placements.createPlacement.js | Creates a placement; optionally links it to a folder via TARS service. |\n| GET `/api/placements/:slug/schedule` | scheduler/placements.scheduler.getPlacementSchedule.js | Returns aggregated live/scheduled/history content for a placement. |\n| POST `/api/placements/:slug/clone` | scheduler/placements.scheduler.clonePlacement.js | Clones a placement (new slug) with optional content items. |\n| GET `/api/placements/:slug/live-content` | scheduler/placements.scheduler.getPlacementLiveContent.js | Fetches the currently-live content item for a placement. |\n| GET `/api/placements/:slug` | scheduler/placements.scheduler.getPlacementBySlug.js | Fetches one placement's config/schema by slug. |\n| PUT `/api/placements/:slug` | scheduler/placements.scheduler.updatePlacement.js | Updates placement schema, or creates a new content item (branches on payload shape). |\n| DELETE `/api/placements/:slug` | scheduler/placements.scheduler.deletePlacement.js | Deletes a placement. |\n| POST `/api/placements/:slug/items` | scheduler/placements.scheduler.createItem.js | Returns a stub/blank unsaved content item (no backend call). |\n| POST `/api/placements/:slug/items/:itemId/duplicate` | scheduler/placements.scheduler.duplicateItem.js | Duplicates a content item, prefixing title \"CLONE - \". |\n| DELETE `/api/placements/:slug/items/:itemId` | scheduler/placements.scheduler.deleteItem.js | Deletes a single content item from a placement. |\n| GET `/api/placements/scheduler/items/metadata/:contentType/:emsId` | scheduler/placements.scheduler.getPlacementListItemMetadata.js | Fetches fresh EMS (+ Critics) metadata for a list item by EMS ID. |\n| GET `/api/placements/scheduler/items/metadata-fid/:contentType/:fandangoId` | backstage/placements.scheduler.getPlacementListItemMetadataByFid.js | Fetches movie metadata via direct Fandango-ID lookup (Discovery service). |\n| GET `/api/placements/scheduler/items/search-title/:contentType` | backstage/placements.scheduler.searchByTitle.js | Searches Backstage globalSearch by title for fd-list-fid item picking. |\n| GET `/api/placements/browse/:placementId` | browse/placements.browse.getFolderByPlacement.js | Returns which folder contains a given placement. |\n| GET `/api/placements/browse/folders/:folderId` | browse/placements.browse.getFolderById.js | Returns a folder's metadata plus child folders/placement IDs. |\n| POST `/api/placements/browse/folders` | browse/placements.browse.createFolder.js | Creates a new folder (optionally under a parent). |\n| PUT `/api/placements/browse/folders/:folderId` | browse/placements.browse.updateFolder.js | Renames and/or moves (reparents) a folder. |\n| DELETE `/api/placements/browse/folders/:folderId` | browse/placements.browse.deleteFolder.js | Deletes a folder. |\n| PUT `/api/placements/browse/folders/:folderId/items/:placementId` | browse/placements.browse.addPlacement.js | Assigns/moves a placement into a folder (drag-and-drop). |\n\n## 3. External services (grouped by handler)\n\n- **PLACEMENT_SERVICE_ENDPOINT** (axios, primary CRUD backend) — used by: getAllPlacements, createPlacement, clonePlacement, deleteItem, deletePlacement, duplicateItem, getPlacementBySlug, getPlacementLiveContent, getPlacementSchedule, updatePlacement.\n- **TARS_SERVICE_ENDPOINT** — used by: createPlacement (folder link), clonePlacement, and all `browse/*` folder handlers (getFolderById, getFolderByPlacement, createFolder, updateFolder, deleteFolder, addPlacement).\n- **EMS_SERVICE_ENDPOINT / EMS_SERVICE_AUTH_TOKEN, CRITICS_SERVICE_ENDPOINT / CRITICS_SERVICE_AUTH_TOKEN** — used by: getPlacementListItemMetadata (EMS ID metadata lookups, plus Critics scores).\n- **DISCOVERY_SERVICE_ENDPOINT** — used by: getPlacementListItemMetadataByFid (backstage/_services/discovery.js), for Fandango-ID movie lookups.\n- **BACKSTAGE_SERVICE_ENDPOINT** — used by: searchByTitle (backstage/_services/backstage.js), for title search via globalSearch.\n- createItem.js calls no external service (stub only).\n\nSo yes — more than one external service: Placement Service, TARS, EMS, Critics, Discovery, and Backstage are all called by the placements module's server handlers.\n\n## 4. Auth / AD-group findings\n\nNo AD-group restriction is applied to `/placements` or `/api/placements/*`. In client `utils/constants.js`, the Placements module entry has no `group` key (unlike RT Critics, User Ratings, EMS, Customer Service which specify `group: 'webtars_...'`), so the nav link and route are visible to any authenticated user. Server-side, `/api/placements/*` routes carry no group/role middleware — only the global `requestContextMiddleware` (decodes JWT into `req.user`, including `groups[]`) and `requestLogger` are applied app-wide; no handler in `src/server/placements` or `src/server/backstage` checks `req.user.groups`. Access is gated only by the client-side `RootLayout`'s `isAuthenticated` check (redirect to `/login`), not by group membership.","usage":{"total_tokens":72643,"tool_uses":29,"duration_ms":112747},"uuid":"04adbc07-f127-4a6f-ad43-ce9b711fb5ec","session_id":"9e77c916-bd20-4e4a-9aa4-d29922bf6a2f"}
