ementLiveContent, getPlacementSchedule, updatePlacement.\n- **TARS_SERVICE_ENDPOINT** — used by: createPlacement (folder link), clonePlacement, and all `browse/*` folder handlers (getFolderById, getFolderByPlacement, createFolder, updateFolder, deleteFolder, addPlacement).\n- **EMS_SERVICE_ENDPOINT / EMS_SERVICE_AUTH_TOKEN, CRITICS_SERVICE_ENDPOINT / CRITICS_SERVICE_AUTH_TOKEN** — used by: getPlacementListItemMetadata (EMS ID metadata lookups, plus Critics scores).\n- **DISCOVERY_SERVICE_ENDPOINT** — used by: getPlacementListItemMetadataByFid (backstage/_services/discovery.js), for Fandango-ID movie lookups.\n- **BACKSTAGE_SERVICE_ENDPOINT** — used by: searchByTitle (backstage/_services/backstage.js), for title search via globalSearch.\n- createItem.js calls no external service (stub only).\n\nSo yes — more than one external service: Placement Service, TARS, EMS, Critics, Discovery, and Backstage are all called by the placements module's server handlers.\n\n## 4. Auth / AD-group findings\n\nNo AD-group restriction is applied to `/placements` or `/api/placements/*`. In client `utils/constants.js`, the Placements module entry has no `group` key (unlike RT Critics, User Ratings, EMS, Customer Service which specify `group: 'webtars_...'`), so the nav link and route are visible to any authenticated user. Server-side, `/api/placements/*` routes carry no group/role middleware — only the global `requestContextMiddleware` (decodes JWT into `req.user`, including `groups[]`) and `requestLogger` are applied app-wide; no handler in `src/server/placements` or `src/server/backstage` checks `req.user.groups`. Access is gated only by the client-side `RootLayout`'s `isAuthenticated` check (redirect to `/login`), not by group membership."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e77c916-bd20-4e4a-9aa4-d29922bf6a2f","uuid":"104605c0-82ba-4301-9d86-fe8d120c45fc","timestamp":"2026-08-02T04:18:48.183Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo /Users/206618626@bwt