{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5utdb7yuujfbz2t7ceoyr7rxwmtxvynr4nzvgm5hwstdrvcpi77q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01LvivTqKPUZ7cbmwiTkayTC","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/206618626@bwt3.com/Desktop/Repos/webtarsthree/docs/modules/placements.md","content":"# Placements\n\n## Purpose\n\nManages content placements for Fandango properties. Provides tools for scheduling, organizing, and previewing editorial content placements across different platform surfaces.\n\n## Access\n\n- **Route:** `/placements`\n- **AD Group:** None — available to all authenticated users\n\n## Features\n\n**Scheduler**\n\n- View and manage placement schedules by slug\n- Create, duplicate, and delete schedule items\n- Clone entire placements\n- Update placement metadata and schemas\n- View live content for a placement\n- Look up item metadata by content type and EMS ID\n\n**Browse / Folders**\n\n- Browse placements organized in folders\n- Create, update, and delete folders\n- Add placements to folders\n\n**Playground**\n\n- Preview and test placement configurations\n\n## External Services\n\n| Service                | Purpose                                                   | Env Var                                                     |\n| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Placement Service       | Core CRUD for placements, schedules, folders                | `PLACEMENT_SERVICE_ENDPOINT`                                    |\n| TARS Service            | Folder linking for placements; all folder CRUD               | `TARS_SERVICE_ENDPOINT`                                         |\n| EMS Service             | Metadata lookups for list items by EMS ID                    | `EMS_SERVICE_ENDPOINT`, `EMS_SERVICE_AUTH_TOKEN`                  |\n| Critics Service         | Critic scores attached to EMS item metadata                  | `CRITICS_SERVICE_ENDPOINT`, `CRITICS_SERVICE_AUTH_TOKEN`          |\n| Discovery Service       | Movie metadata lookups by Fandango ID (fd-list-fid items)    | `DISCOVERY_SERVICE_ENDPOINT`                                    |\n| Backstage Service       | Title search for picking fd-list-fid items                   | `BACKSTAGE_SERVICE_ENDPOINT`                                    |\n\n## Key Business Rules\n\n- **Slugs:** Placements are identified by slug (URL-friendly identifier), not numeric IDs.\n- **Schemas:** Each placement has a configurable schema that defines the shape of its content items.\n- **Cloning:** Entire placements can be cloned for creating variations or staging.\n- **Live content:** The scheduler shows what's currently live vs scheduled for each placement.\n- **Folder organization:** Placements are organized into a folder hierarchy for browsing.\n\n## Structure\n\n- Client: `src/client/pages/placements/` — `scheduler/`, `folders/`, `playground/`, `_shared/`\n- Server: `src/server/placements/` — `scheduler/`, `browse/`\n\n## Client Routes\n\n| Route | Page | Description |\n| ----- | ---- | ------------ |\n| `/placements` | `PlacementsPage` | Landing page for the module; shows recent placement history with a \"clear history\" action. |\n| `/placements/playground` | `PlaygroundPage` | Sandbox to build/preview a JSON-schema + UI-schema and live-preview the generated form (no server persistence). |\n| `/placements/create` | `PlacementsCreatePage` | Form to create a new placement, choosing a type (form / list / fd-list / fd-list-fid). |\n| `/placements/browse` | `PlacementsBrowsePage` (redirect) | Redirects to `/placements/browse/1` (root folder). |\n| `/placements/browse/1` | `PlacementsBrowsePage` | Root folder view — folder browser with drag-and-drop for organizing placements into folders/subfolders. |\n| `/placements/browse/:folderId` | `PlacementsBrowsePage` | Folder browser for a specific folder, same drag-and-drop organization. |\n| `/placements/scheduler/form/:slug` | `SchedulerFormPage` | Editor for a schema-driven \"form\" type placement — edit content/schema tabs, view live/scheduled/history. |\n| `/placements/scheduler/json/:slug` | `SchedulerJsonPage` | Raw JSON editor variant of the placement editor (content/schema tabs via JSON). |\n| `/placements/scheduler/list/:slug` | `SchedulerListPage` | Editor for \"list\" type placements — drag-and-drop ordered content list. |\n| `/placements/scheduler/fd-list/:slug` | `SchedulerListPage` | Same list editor, used for Fandango/Vudu-flavored list placements (`ui: 'fd-list'`). |\n| `/placements/scheduler/fd-list-fid/:slug` | `SchedulerListPage` | Same list editor for the FID-lookup list variant (`ui: 'fd-list-fid'`), items resolved by Fandango ID. |\n\n## Server Routes\n\n| Method | Path | Handler | Purpose |\n| ------ | ---- | ------- | ------- |\n| GET | `/api/placements` | `placementsBrowseGetAllPlacementsHandler` | Lists all placements, optional `?name=` filter, via Placement Service. |\n| POST | `/api/placements` | `placementsCreatePlacementHandler` | Creates a placement; optionally links it to a folder via TARS service. |\n| GET | `/api/placements/:slug/schedule` | `placementsSchedulerGetPlacementScheduleHandler` | Returns aggregated live/scheduled/history content for a placement. |\n| POST | `/api/placements/:slug/clone` | `placementsSchedulerClonePlacementHandler` | Clones a placement (new slug) with optional content items. |\n| GET | `/api/placements/:slug/live-content` | `placementsSchedulerGetPlacementLiveContentHandler` | Fetches the currently-live content item for a placement. |\n| GET | `/api/placements/:slug` | `placementsSchedulerGetPlacementBySlugHandler` | Fetches one placement's config/schema by slug. |\n| PUT | `/api/placements/:slug` | `placementsSchedulerUpdatePlacementHandler` | Updates placement schema, or creates a new content item (branches on payload shape). |\n| DELETE | `/api/placements/:slug` | `placementsSchedulerDeletePlacementHandler` | Deletes a placement. |\n| POST | `/api/placements/:slug/items` | `placementsSchedulerCreateItemHandler` | Returns a stub/blank unsaved content item (no backend call). |\n| POST | `/api/placements/:slug/items/:itemId/duplicate` | `placementsSchedulerDuplicateItemHandler` | Duplicates a content item, prefixing title \"CLONE - \". |\n| DELETE | `/api/placements/:slug/items/:itemId` | `placementsSchedulerDeleteItemHandler` | Deletes a single content item from a placement. |\n| GET | `/api/placements/scheduler/items/metadata/:contentType/:emsId` | `placementsSchedulerGetPlacementListItemMetadataHandler` | Fetches fresh EMS (+ Critics) metadata for a list item by EMS ID. |\n| GET | `/api/placements/scheduler/items/metadata-fid/:contentType/:fandangoId` | `placementsSchedulerGetPlacementListItemMetadataByFidHandler` | Fetches movie metadata via direct Fandango ID lookup (Discovery service). |\n| GET | `/api/placements/scheduler/items/search-title/:contentType` | `placementsSchedulerSearchByTitleHandler` | Searches Backstage globalSearch by title for fd-list-fid item picking. |\n| GET | `/api/placements/browse/:placementId` | `placementsBrowseGetFolderByPlacementHandler` | Returns which folder contains a given placement. |\n| GET | `/api/placements/browse/folders/:folderId` | `placementsBrowseGetFolderByIdHandler` | Returns a folder's metadata plus child folders/placement IDs. |\n| POST | `/api/placements/browse/folders` | `placementsBrowseCreateFolderHandler` | Creates a new folder (optionally under a parent). |\n| PUT | `/api/placements/browse/folders/:folderId` | `placementsBrowseUpdateFolderHandler` | Renames and/or moves (reparents) a folder. |\n| DELETE | `/api/placements/browse/folders/:folderId` | `placementsBrowseDeleteFolderHandler` | Deletes a folder. |\n| PUT | `/api/placements/browse/folders/:folderId/items/:placementId` | `placementsBrowseAddPlacementHandler` | Assigns/moves a placement into a folder (drag-and-drop). |\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- **AD Group:** None — `/placements` and all `/api/placements/*` routes are open to any authenticated user. Access is gated only by the client-side authentication check, not by group membership.\n- **External services:** Placement Service (`PLACEMENT_SERVICE_ENDPOINT`), TARS Service (`TARS_SERVICE_ENDPOINT`), EMS Service (`EMS_SERVICE_ENDPOINT`, `EMS_SERVICE_AUTH_TOKEN`), Critics Service (`CRITICS_SERVICE_ENDPOINT`, `CRITICS_SERVICE_AUTH_TOKEN`), Discovery Service (`DISCOVERY_SERVICE_ENDPOINT`), Backstage Service (`BACKSTAGE_SERVICE_ENDPOINT`).\n\n## Working Here\n\n**Module structure:**\n\nPlacements has three sub-features (scheduler, folders, playground) and shared utilities in `_shared/`. The shared folder contains components, hooks, drag utilities, RJSF (React JSON Schema Form) config, and a placement validator.\n\n**Read first:**\n\n1. `PlacementsPage.jsx` — landing page with placement list\n2. `scheduler/SchedulerListPage.jsx` — the most complex sub-feature\n3. `_shared/rjsfConfig.js` — RJSF configuration for schema-driven forms\n4. `_shared/placementUtils.js` — shared utility functions\n\n**Adding a new placement feature:**\n\n1. Create `src/client/pages/placements/{feature}/` following `scheduler/` or `folders/` as reference\n2. Add shared components to `_shared/components/` if reusable\n3. Server handlers go in `src/server/placements/{feature}/`\n4. Wire routes in `src/server/app.js` under the Placements section\n\n**Server-side pattern:**\n\nAll handlers call the Placement Service via `PLACEMENT_SERVICE_ENDPOINT`. Server is split into `scheduler/` and `browse/` matching the client-side feature split.\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1418,"cache_read_input_tokens":78205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1418,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e77c916-bd20-4e4a-9aa4-d29922bf6a2f","uuid":"692a58d5-9393-4442-b766-221a61c0286a","timestamp":"2026-08-02T04:19:26.765Z","request_id":"bedrock-1785644337526-xlnd"}
